{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794315462989,"sessionID":"ses_e3a801e1dffegVWZJ0Q16Bat5g","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_0Sra6bHNL6ne5mjyOPE4uoa8","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx\n@@\n function storedSession(): Session | null {\n@@\n }\n \n+function persistSession(session: Session | null) {\n+  try {\n+    if (session) localStorage.setItem(\"base64-session\", JSON.stringify(session));\n+    else localStorage.removeItem(\"base64-session\");\n+  } catch { return; }\n+}\n+\n@@\n-    try { localStorage.removeItem(\"base64-session\"); } catch { /* */ }\n+    persistSession(null);\n@@\n-    try { localStorage.setItem(\"base64-session\", JSON.stringify(next)); } catch { /* */ }\n+    persistSession(next);\n*** Update File: /workspace/frontend/src/icons.tsx\n@@\n+import type { ReactNode } from \"react\";\n+\n@@\n-const paths: Record<IconName, React.ReactNode> = {\n+const paths: Record<IconName, ReactNode> = {\n*** Update File: /workspace/README.md\n@@\n-# App\n+# Base64\n@@\n-Dependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n+Dependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and hashes and is installed directly with pip. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well.\n+\n+## Development\n+\n+Use Python 3.13 and Node 24. From the workspace root:\n+\n+```sh\n+python3 -m venv backend/.venv\n+backend/.venv/bin/pip install -r backend/requirements.lock\n+backend/.venv/bin/gunicorn --bind 0.0.0.0:8000 --pythonpath backend app:app\n+```\n+\n+In a separate terminal, from `frontend/`:\n+\n+```sh\n+npm ci\n+npm run dev\n+```\n+\n+Vite proxies `/api` to port 8000. Run `npm run build` in `frontend/` to build the frontend; Flask then serves that build on port 8000.\n+\n+## Checks\n+\n+From `frontend/`:\n+\n+```sh\n+npm run lint\n+npm run typecheck\n+npm run build\n+```\n+\n+From the workspace root:\n+\n+```sh\n+backend/.venv/bin/python -m unittest discover -s backend -v\n+backend/.venv/bin/pip install ruff\n+backend/.venv/bin/ruff check backend\n+```\n+\n+## API\n+\n+All request bodies are JSON objects. Errors return `{\"error\": \"message\"}` with an appropriate HTTP status.\n+\n+| Method | Endpoint | Body / behavior |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| GET | `/api/health` | Returns `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` |\n+| POST | `/api/auth/register` | `{\"username\": \"you\", \"password\": \"your-password\"}`; creates an account (201) |\n+| POST | `/api/auth/login` | Same body; returns `{\"token\": \"...\"}` |\n+| GET | `/api/auth/me` | Returns the authenticated username |\n+| POST | `/api/auth/logout` | Invalidates the current token (204) |\n+| POST | `/api/base64/encode` | `{\"text\": \"Hello\"}`; returns `{\"encoded\": \"SGVsbG8=\"}`; never saves |\n+| POST | `/api/base64/decode` | `{\"encoded\": \"SGVsbG8=\"}`; returns `{\"text\": \"Hello\"}`; never saves |\n+| POST | `/api/conversions` | `{\"direction\": \"encode\", \"input\": \"Hello\"}`; converts, saves, and returns the conversion including full `output` (201) |\n+| GET | `/api/conversions?page=1&page_size=10` | Returns `items`, `total`, `page`, and `page_size`; newest first |\n+| DELETE | `/api/conversions/{id}` | Deletes an owned conversion (204), otherwise 404 |\n+\n+Account and history requests require `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. Tokens expire after 30 days, are stored only as SHA-256 hashes on the server, and remain valid across restarts. Passwords use Werkzeug's scrypt hashing. Usernames are unique without regard to case.\n+\n+Conversions contain `id`, `direction`, `input_preview`, `output_preview`, and UTC `created_at`. Previews are limited to 160 characters; only creation responses include the full output. Pagination defaults to page 1 with 10 items; `page_size` must be between 1 and 100.\n+\n+Encoding accepts empty text and all valid UTF-8. Decoding requires canonical standard Base64 with padding, no whitespace, and valid UTF-8 decoded bytes. Base64 is not encryption. Request bodies are limited to 2 MiB.\n+\n+SQLite data is stored in `./data/base64.sqlite3`. Mount `/app/data` as a persistent volume when running the image. Set `DATA_DIR` to override the data directory during local development or tests.\n+\n+```sh\n+docker build -t base64 .\n+docker run --rm -p 8000:8000 -v base64-data:/app/data base64\n+```\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM frontend/src/App.tsx\nM frontend/src/icons.tsx\nM README.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx\n+++ /workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx\n@@ -12,8 +12,15 @@\n     return value && typeof value.token === \"string\" && typeof value.username === \"string\" ? value : null;\n   } catch { return null; }\n }\n \n+function persistSession(session: Session | null) {\n+  try {\n+    if (session) localStorage.setItem(\"base64-session\", JSON.stringify(session));\n+    else localStorage.removeItem(\"base64-session\");\n+  } catch { return; }\n+}\n+\n const features = [\n   { icon: \"globe\" as const, title: \"Every character welcome.\", description: \"UTF-8 text, emojis, and everything in between.\" },\n   { icon: \"shield\" as const, title: \"Private by default.\", description: \"Nothing is saved unless you choose to save it.\" },\n   { icon: \"bolt\" as const, title: \"Less friction. More flow.\", description: \"No signup needed. Just paste, convert, and go.\" },\n@@ -40,9 +47,9 @@\n \n   const clearSession = useCallback(() => {\n     setSession(null);\n     setSave(false);\n-    try { localStorage.removeItem(\"base64-session\"); } catch { /* */ }\n+    persistSession(null);\n   }, []);\n \n   const sessionExpired = useCallback(() => {\n     clearSession();\n@@ -74,9 +81,9 @@\n   }, []);\n \n   function authenticated(next: Session) {\n     setSession(next);\n-    try { localStorage.setItem(\"base64-session\", JSON.stringify(next)); } catch { /* */ }\n+    persistSession(next);\n     setAuthMode(null);\n     setError(\"\");\n     setNotice(\"You're signed in. Make yourself at home.\");\n   }\n\nIndex: /workspace/frontend/src/icons.tsx\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/frontend/src/icons.tsx\n+++ /workspace/frontend/src/icons.tsx\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n type IconName = \"arrow\" | \"swap\" | \"copy\" | \"check\" | \"close\" | \"history\" | \"lock\" | \"code\" | \"globe\" | \"shield\" | \"bolt\" | \"chevron\" | \"trash\" | \"logout\" | \"clipboard\" | \"info\" | \"plus\" | \"user\";\n \n-const paths: Record<IconName, React.ReactNode> = {\n+const paths: Record<IconName, ReactNode> = {\n   arrow: <><path d=\"M4 12h16m-6-6 6 6-6 6\" /></>,\n   swap: <><path d=\"M4 7h16m-4-4 4 4-4 4M20 17H4m4-4-4 4 4 4\" /></>,\n   copy: <><rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" rx=\"2\" /><path d=\"M15 8V5a2 2 0 0 0-2-2H5a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h3\" /></>,\n   check: <path d=\"m5 12 4 4L19 6\" />,\n@@ -23,4 +23,5 @@\n \n export default function Icon({ name, className = \"h-4 w-4\" }: { name: IconName; className?: string }) {\n   return <svg aria-hidden=\"true\" className={className} viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" strokeWidth=\"1.65\" strokeLinecap=\"round\" strokeLinejoin=\"round\">{paths[name]}</svg>;\n }\n+import type { ReactNode } from \"react\";\n\nIndex: /workspace/README.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/README.md\n+++ /workspace/README.md\n@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@\n-# App\n+# Base64\n \n ## Run contract\n \n - The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n@@ -11,5 +11,72 @@\n \n - `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n - `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n \n-Dependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n+Dependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and hashes and is installed directly with pip. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well.\n+\n+## Development\n+\n+Use Python 3.13 and Node 24. From the workspace root:\n+\n+```sh\n+python3 -m venv backend/.venv\n+backend/.venv/bin/pip install -r backend/requirements.lock\n+backend/.venv/bin/gunicorn --bind 0.0.0.0:8000 --pythonpath backend app:app\n+```\n+\n+In a separate terminal, from `frontend/`:\n+\n+```sh\n+npm ci\n+npm run dev\n+```\n+\n+Vite proxies `/api` to port 8000. Run `npm run build` in `frontend/` to build the frontend; Flask then serves that build on port 8000.\n+\n+## Checks\n+\n+From `frontend/`:\n+\n+```sh\n+npm run lint\n+npm run typecheck\n+npm run build\n+```\n+\n+From the workspace root:\n+\n+```sh\n+backend/.venv/bin/python -m unittest discover -s backend -v\n+backend/.venv/bin/pip install ruff\n+backend/.venv/bin/ruff check backend\n+```\n+\n+## API\n+\n+All request bodies are JSON objects. Errors return `{\"error\": \"message\"}` with an appropriate HTTP status.\n+\n+| Method | Endpoint | Body / behavior |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| GET | `/api/health` | Returns `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` |\n+| POST | `/api/auth/register` | `{\"username\": \"you\", \"password\": \"your-password\"}`; creates an account (201) |\n+| POST | `/api/auth/login` | Same body; returns `{\"token\": \"...\"}` |\n+| GET | `/api/auth/me` | Returns the authenticated username |\n+| POST | `/api/auth/logout` | Invalidates the current token (204) |\n+| POST | `/api/base64/encode` | `{\"text\": \"Hello\"}`; returns `{\"encoded\": \"SGVsbG8=\"}`; never saves |\n+| POST | `/api/base64/decode` | `{\"encoded\": \"SGVsbG8=\"}`; returns `{\"text\": \"Hello\"}`; never saves |\n+| POST | `/api/conversions` | `{\"direction\": \"encode\", \"input\": \"Hello\"}`; converts, saves, and returns the conversion including full `output` (201) |\n+| GET | `/api/conversions?page=1&page_size=10` | Returns `items`, `total`, `page`, and `page_size`; newest first |\n+| DELETE | `/api/conversions/{id}` | Deletes an owned conversion (204), otherwise 404 |\n+\n+Account and history requests require `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. Tokens expire after 30 days, are stored only as SHA-256 hashes on the server, and remain valid across restarts. Passwords use Werkzeug's scrypt hashing. Usernames are unique without regard to case.\n+\n+Conversions contain `id`, `direction`, `input_preview`, `output_preview`, and UTC `created_at`. Previews are limited to 160 characters; only creation responses include the full output. Pagination defaults to page 1 with 10 items; `page_size` must be between 1 and 100.\n+\n+Encoding accepts empty text and all valid UTF-8. Decoding requires canonical standard Base64 with padding, no whitespace, and valid UTF-8 decoded bytes. Base64 is not encryption. Request bodies are limited to 2 MiB.\n+\n+SQLite data is stored in `./data/base64.sqlite3`. Mount `/app/data` as a persistent volume when running the image. Set `DATA_DIR` to override the data directory during local development or tests.\n+\n+```sh\n+docker build -t base64 .\n+docker run --rm -p 8000:8000 -v base64-data:/app/data base64\n+```\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx","relativePath":"frontend/src/App.tsx","type":"update","patch":"Index: /workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx\n